{"id":"u-65150764-a469-458c-ba8b-a66beb4e00fe","src":"community","title":"The Comeback - Strength at 40","author":"David Demonio","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/fBovJ0-mr-thrickstr-50-1","desc":"The true purpose of this program is twofold:\n\nTransition from a sedentary lifestyle in your 40s and built your consistent lifting habit.  Habit creation is the hardest part at this age so this is important:\nYou won't always feel 100%, but showing up still counts. On tough days, commit to doing just one set. A minimal effort beats a zero every single time.\n\nThe Physical Strategy: Structurally, its purpose is to build maximum upper and lower body strength using minimal equipment (strictly dumbbells, a bench, and a pull-up bar). It achieves this by forcing heavy neurological strength adaptations on your main compound lifts, paired with high-efficiency, joint-friendly muscle growth via your 15-second rest-pause finishers.\n\n\nPURPOSE: To build maximal strength and muscle density using minimal gear, honoring joint longevity and recovery.\n\n1. THE STRENGTH BLOCKS (Exercises 1 & 2 of each week)\n\nGoal: Build raw power and neurological strength.\n\nExecution: Use maximum weight for 4–6 reps (6–8 for legs) with perfect form. Leave 1–2 reps \"in the tank\" on early sets to avoid dangerous failure.\nRemember, failure is the point where your muscles literally cannot complete another full rep with good form.\n\n\n\nRest: Strictly rest 2 to 3 minutes between these sets. Full recovery is required to lift heavy.\n\n2. THE REST-PAUSE BLOCKS (Exercises 3, 4, & 5)\n\nGoal: Maximize muscle growth and efficiency while protecting joints.\n\nExecution: Pick a weight where you hit absolute failure around 10–12 reps.\n\nPacing: After a set, count a 15-second rest, go to failure again, count a 15-second rest, and go to failure a final time.\n\n3. THE GOLDEN RULES\n\nDay 7 is non-negotiable REST. No dumbbells, no heavy cardio. Let the central nervous system and joint cartilage fully recover.\n\nTrack Progression: Focus on progressive overload.  Try to add 1 rep or a slight weight increase to your heavy Strength Blocks every single week.","level":["Novice"],"goals":["Strength","Muscle"],"equipment":["Dumbbell Only"],"minutes":30,"joins":4,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-04T11:11:01.520Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4","Day 5","Day 6","Day 7"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Dip (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":4}]},{"n":"One Arm Bent Over Row","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Concentration Curl","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Goblet Squat","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Shrug (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]}]},{"n":"Reverse Abs Crunch (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Dip (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":4}]},{"n":"One Arm Bent Over Row","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Concentration Curl","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Goblet Squat","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (D